# Supply-chain policy for third-party dependencies.
# A 7-day release-age quarantine means `pnpm update --latest` deliberately
# resolves older than the registry's newest version; that gap is correct.
# The trust policy refuses any version whose provenance is weaker than an
# earlier version of the same package, and git/URL deps are blocked anywhere in
# the transitive tree. An ERR_PNPM_TRUST_DOWNGRADE is investigated and, when
# benign, waived for one exact name@version under `trustPolicyExclude` in
# pnpm-workspace.yaml — pnpm 10's yaml key REPLACES `trust-policy-exclude[]`,
# so waivers live there, never here. Never bypass with `--config.trust-policy=accept`.

strict-peer-dependencies=true
engine-strict=true
minimum-release-age=10080
trust-policy=no-downgrade
block-exotic-subdeps=true
